Strategy Guidance:
Design your algorithm to maintain a population of candidate solutions. At each step, balance exploration (probing new regions of the search space) and exploitation (refining the most promising solutions found so far).

Implement your algorithm using NumPy matrix operations on populations of shape `(pop_size, dim)` — batch candidate generation, batch evaluation, and vectorized updates — rather than scalar Python loops over individual solutions.

Algorithm families that excel on continuous deterministic BBOB landscapes:
- Differential Evolution (DE/rand/1/bin or DE/current-to-best/1): vectors `v = x_r1 + F * (x_r2 - x_r3)` with binomial crossover.
- Covariance Matrix Adaptation / Adaptive Step-size search: adapting search distributions towards successful update vectors.
- Hybrid Global-Local search: global population exploration followed by local pattern search around top candidates.

A concrete vectorized update pattern:
    mutants = pop[r1] + F * (pop[r2] - pop[r3])
    mask = np.random.rand(pop_size, dim) < CR
    trials = np.where(mask, mutants, pop)
